<title>LITHUANIA: Lithuanian three-mth T-bill rate rises further.</title>
<headline>Lithuanian three-mth T-bill rate rises further.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield for Lithuanian 94-day Treasury bills rose to 13.06 percent at auction on Friday from 12.67 percent at a sale of 88-day paper yesterday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>All amounts are in millions of litas.</p>
<p> MATURITY   AV YIELD   LAST TIME   MIN/MAX   ISSUE  BID  SOLD</p>
<p>  94-day     13.06	12.67     12.0/13.81  45   80.215 45</p>
<p>Settlement date for today's auction is December 24 and the bills mature on March 28.</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
